FYI, I also just tried the default parameterization = "delta", but also set start = TRUE, and my example returns nonzero factor loadings (and residual variances therefore differ from 1) without a warning about NPD covariance matrix of model parameters:

fit.delta.start <- efaUnrotate(datCat[1:8], nf = 2, start=TRUE)
summary(fit.delta.start)

This means the starting values from the factanal() function allows the optimizer to find a better solution than using lavaan's default starting values (i.e., the ones it uses when users provide none).  I am stymied, but at least we know it can still work.  I will add a warning for this specific scenario, with instructions for how users can fix it (either change parameterization= or set start = TRUE).

