I try to learn more about RMSEA and SRMR. I know that if the sample size of my study increases, RMSEA will decrease (David Kenny, 2015) <http://davidakenny.net/cm/fit.htm>. How about SRMR?  From Kenny's website, he said that SRMR is a positively biased measure and that bias is greater for small N and for low df studies because the SRMR is an absolute measure of fit, a value of zero indicates perfect fit. Does it mean small N or low df will have low value of SRMR as a result? What if I have a good result of SRMR(e.g. <0.06) and a poor result of RMSEA(e.g. >0.08)?  Should I collect more data for it? Thank you so much.

